# EXISTING PRODUCT IS REFERENCE, NOT A PRISON

Study existing patterns carefully.

Classify them internally as:

### GOOD

Suitable for reuse.

### ACCEPTABLE

Can be reused when context matches.

### LEGACY

Maintain when necessary but avoid spreading into new work.

### PROBLEMATIC

Should not be copied merely for consistency.

Do not preserve a weak UX pattern only because it already exists.

Do not replace a good pattern only because something newer exists.

The goal is controlled evolution.

