# PROJECT EVOLUTION PRINCIPLE

This project will continue changing.

Future work may involve:

* new pages
* removed pages
* redesigned workflows
* new components
* replaced components
* new packages
* removed packages
* new APIs
* new interaction patterns
* new design-system primitives
* new responsive requirements
* new business requirements

Therefore:

Do not freeze today's implementation into permanent rules.

Instead preserve stable DESIGN PRINCIPLES.

When a new pattern is clearly better:

1. verify that the existing pattern does not adequately solve the requirement
2. introduce the new pattern intentionally
3. adapt it to the current visual language
4. evaluate whether it should become reusable
5. avoid unnecessary parallel patterns
6. document the decision when it becomes a project convention
7. update relevant AI rules/skills when appropriate

Do not change things for novelty.

Do not preserve poor solutions merely for consistency.

